ors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 34 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a 7 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm breast excisional biopsy specimen  with an attached 5 x 0 8cm skin ellipse  The entire specimen is inked black  with the deep margin  posterior  overinked blue  and the superior margin overinked red  It is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a tan gray  1 2cm in largest dimension  firm mass  focally abutting the anterior soft tissue margin  and 0 5cm from the posterior margin  Sectioning of the tissue away from the mass reveals a 0 6cm in largest dimension area of tan grittiness  coming to within 0 3cm of the deep margin  in the medial portion of the specimen  There is a third area of grittiness  0 2cm in largest dimension  coming to within 0 6cm of the deep margin  The remainder of the tissue is mixed white fibrous parenchyma and fatty tissue  SECTION CODE A C  Firm nodule with anterior and posterior margins  D  Representative section of nodule  E  Gritty area  F  Second gritty area  G H  Representative sections  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   LUMPECTOMY  AREA SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA CLOSE TO ANTERIOR MARGIN  O R  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Positive.
