AL FINDINGS   2 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU TUMOR SIZE  Spanning at least 1 7cm  GRADE  3  CALCIFICATIONS  In the carcinoma in situ and in benign changes  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Present at the margin of the specimen in several foci  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm portion of gray white to tan pink fibroadipose tissue with a short black stitch designating the anterior margin  a long black stitch the lateral  and a bowtie stitch the cephalad margin  The posterior margin is inked black  the anterior blue  the lateral yellow  and the medial green  The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a diffusely dense gray white fibrous cut surface with a fairly well delineated REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm solid rubbery gray white nodule which abuts the posterior margin along the mid lateral aspect of the specimen  Located 2 5cm superomedial to the fibrous nodule is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm firm area which comes to 0 1cm of the medial margin along the anterior aspect  The remaining fibrous tissue shows focal nodularity  Representative sections are submitted from superior to inferior as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gritty focus along anteromedial aspect   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Rubbery nodule  entirely submitted    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative diffusely nodular fibrous tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections  particularly along the medial margin  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional left breast tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of gray white to tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with no orientation  The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal a poorly delineated REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm indurated gra