ng of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm segment of fibrofatty breast tissue with localization wire  Inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 6cm tan  firm nodular area that extends to within 0 1cm of the inked margin grossly  A second 0 6cm fragment of tan  fibrofatty tissue is present  this is inked and sectioned to reveal a tan yellow unremarkable tissue  The specimens are submitted entirely in cassettes A through L  with suspicious area in A  and the second fragment of tissue entirely in L  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  AREA GROSSLY HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  DAVID SABLE  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Simon Bergman  MD O R  Staff Pathologist  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION   report_end  , Positive.
