e binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 06 46 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 11 0cm overlying skin ellipse and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  The superior border of the skin ellipse is marked with a stitch  A 1 0cm in diameter  brown plaque is located at 6 0cm lateral and superior to the nipple  overlying a firm mass below the skin  The resection margins are inked black  the anterior superior resection surface is double inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE tan to white  firm mass located beneath the skin lesion that extends to within 0 2cm of the posterior resection margin  The mass has a 1 0cm diameter irregular shaped cystic cavity containing white mucoid fluids  A 2 0cm in diameter white nodular mass is located at 5 0cm lateral to the first lesion  and appears well circumscribed  extends to within 0 2cm from the posterior resection margin  The second mass is located directly beneath the lateral end of the skin ellipse  at the base of the axillary tail  Section code  A  first mass at its closest resection margin  deep  B  first mass at skin C and D  sections taken from the medial and the lateral portion of the first mass  respectively E  second mass at its nearest resection margin  deep  F  the medial most section of the second mass G  the lateral most section of the second mass H L  nodes from axillary tail Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSIO