MOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  The edges of this cavity are irregular with focal yellow  chalky fatty tissues intermixed  The portion that appears to be biopsy cavity is inked blue  whereas the surrounding exterior of both of these fragments is inked black  Representative sections of the small tissue fragment with adjacent skin are submitted in cassettes A through C  On sectioning  the wall of the biopsy cavity shows white  rubbery  fibrotic tissue as well as flecks of yellow chalky tissue  In addition  focal yellow white speckles are seen within the breast parenchyma away from the main cavity  The entire larger piece is submitted in cassettes D through R  Labeled  axillary dissection tissue   is an aggregate of fibroadipose tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  Multiple lymph nodes are found within this tissue  ranging in size from 0 3cm in greatest diameter up to 1 1cm  On cut surface  they are tan pink to slightly yellow and soft  All or half of each node identified are submitted in cassettes F through V  Resident  C  Diana Jordan  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Andrew Louis Warshaw  M D  Dean M Donahue  M D  PART A  AXILLARY DISSECTION TISSUE  LEFT  PART B  BREAST TISSUE  LEFT    report_end  , Positive.
