Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 49 CLINICAL DATA  Status post needle localization      REVISED REPORT     Reason for Revision  CORRECTED ADDENDUM TISSUE SITE Revised by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Revised on 22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 19                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA GRADE REMOVED_DATE CM  85   EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBRIFORM TYPE  15   CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Edited by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 01                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 02    REVISED REMOVED_DATE    GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal an approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm ill defined  firm area with white streaks  abutting the closest inked surface  corresponding to area of architectural distortion  Area too small to be frozen  Suspicious area submitted in cassette A  the remainder of the specimen in cassettes B through J  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST LEFT  SMALL FOCUS SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA BUT TOO SMALL TO BE FROZEN  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Positive.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D  Resident  Omer Yilmaz  M D   Ph D  Frozen Section Pathologist  Rajni V Mandal  M D  Frozen Section Resident  Devon Gimbel  M D  Signed Out by  John H Eichhorn  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Locally advanced triple negative invasive ductal carcinoma of the left breast  status post neoadjuvant chemotherapy  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST AND AXILLARY TISSUE  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  SLIGHT FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  CELLULAR CHANGES CONSISTENT WITH NEOADJUVANT CHEMOTHERAPY EFFECT  NO RESIDUAL CARCINOMA CELLS ARE IDENTIFIED WITHIN THE BREAST PARENCHYMA  METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA  WITHIN 4 OF 4 NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  All of the candidate lymph nodes that are dissected from the modified radical mastectomy specimen and from the separately submitted left axillary tissue specimen have the appearance of fibroinflammatory nodules containing histiocytes  plasma cells  necrotic cellular material and focal hemosiderin deposits  Very rare isolated viable appearing tumor cells are identified in these nodules  Although the number of residual tumor cells is very small  the appearance is consistent with lymph nodes that may have been largely or completely replaced by tumor before chemotherapy treatment  Because of scarring  the presence or absence of extranodal extension cannot be assessed  No residual tumor cells are identified within the breast parenchyma  which has been extensively sampled for microscopic examination  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY  ADDITIONAL   REGIONAL DISSECTION  METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA  WITHIN 5 OF 5 NODES  SEE NOTE ABOVE  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  SLIGHT FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY WITHIN THE BREAST  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE INCLUDED LYMPH NODE  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY  SENTINEL   315   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  NOTE  Results of immunostains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2  cytokeratin 7  and pankeratin on three tissue levels support the above interpretation  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right sentinel node  315   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fragment of fibrofatty soft tissue  with one REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm lymph node that is frozen entirely as FX 1 and is now submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right simple mastectomy   is a 27 x 18 x 5cm oriented right simple mastectomy specimen  with a short stitch designating the superior and a long stitch designating the lateral margins  The anterior surface contains a 23 x 10 5cm light brown skin ellipse with a 3 5cm in diameter areola and a 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm nipple  which are grossly unremarkable  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a predominantly tan yellow  lobulated cut surface interspersed with moderate fibrous tissue  No discrete mass or lesion is appreciated  The upper outer quadrant tissue is palpated for lymph nodes and no lymph nodes are grossly appreciated  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of breast parenchyma  upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of breast parenchyma from lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of breast parenchyma from lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of breast parenchyma from upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of breast parenchyma from central quadrant  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left modified radical mastectomy   is a 26 x 20 x 5 5cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x 7 x 3cm axillary tail  The specimen is oriented with a short stitch indicating the superior aspect and a long stitch indicating the lateral aspect of the specimen  The specimen is surfaced by a 23 x 10 5cm tan pink skin ellipse with a 4 x 3cm dark brown areola with an inverted nipple  Located 3cm medial to the areola is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm dark brown discoloration  consistent with a previous biopsy site that is 1 5cm to the closest skin margin  No other scars or other skin lesions are grossly appreciated  The anterior resection margin is inked blue  and the posterior resection margin is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm firm indurated mass that is 1 5cm to the closest posterior margin and 4 8cm to the closest anterior margin  The mass is located in the central to lower inner quadrant of the breast  and immediately anterior to the mass  there is a 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm area of fibrous tissue  The remaining mammary tissue is fibrofatty with moderate amounts of fibrous and diffusely nodular tissue  Sectioning of the axillary tail reveals 3 candidate lymph nodes ranging in greatest dimension from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of mass to closest posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remaining small portion of mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire nipple to underlying breast parenchyma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire skin biopsy site to closest skin margin  radially   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of centrally located fibrous tissue to areola   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 candidate lymph node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 candidate lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 candidate lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 candidate lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of breast parenchyma from lower inner quadrant away from mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of breast parenchyma from lower outer quadrant away from mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections from area surrounding mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections from central areas of breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections from upper outer quadrant  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  additional left axillary contents   are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue that aggregate to REMOVED_DATE x 4 x 0 6cm  5 candidate lymph nodes are identified that range in greatest dimension from REMOVED_DATE to 1 2cm  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 candidate lymph node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 candidate lymph node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   3 candidate lymph nodes  INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1  RIGHT AXILLA SENTINEL  315  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 17   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 11 54 31AM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Lymph Node  Right Axilla   Sentinel   315   Excision PART B  Breast  Right   Simple Mastectomy PART C  Breast  Left   Modified Radical Mastectomy PART D  Lymph Nodes  Left Axilla additional   Dissection PART E  Cryostat Frozen Section  slide only   report_end  , Negative.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 56 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  REMOVED_DATE CM EXTENDING TO THE POSTERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL SPECIMEN  1  DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FLORID  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL SPECIMEN  2  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL SPECIMEN  3  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA INVOLVING A SINGLE TERMINAL DUCT LOBULAR UNIT  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 41                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 06 49 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm oriented breast biopsy  The specimen is inked as follows  the medial half   black  lateral half   blue  posterior surface   green over blue or black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a 0 8cm in maximum diameter white gray firm stellate nodule abutting the posteromedial resection margin  A representative section of tumor with posteromedial margin is frozen as FX 1  now submitted in A  The tumor is entirely submitted in A D  Additional breast parenchyma is submitted in E H  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   1   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm piece of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue  bisected and entirely submitted in I  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   2  are two pieces of tan yellow fibroadipose breast tissue  each REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  The pieces are submitted entirely in J  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   3   are two pieces of tan yellow fibroadipose breast tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  respectively  Each is submitted in K and L  respectively  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST   INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA TO POSTERIOR MARGIN  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnos