lts of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 MAY 98 at 12 58 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a mastectomy specimen measuring 20 x 20 x 8cm with an ellipse of skin measuring 10 x 7cm and unremarkable nipple area  Along the medial surface of the specimen there is an area measuring 8 x 8cm that looks like a cystic wall and is focally calcified  Sectioning reveals diffuse  white to hemorrhagic  soft areas occupying about 40  of the total specimen  and present on the posterior inked margin  along the broad front  8 x 6cm    White  soft material is being released from this area upon applying pressure  SECTION CODE A C  Comedo like tumor on the posterior inked margin  E G  Firm  white  focally hemorrhagic area  H  Firm  white area with closest posterior margin  I  Unremarkable breast tissue  J  Skin with adjacent unremarkable breast  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast skin excess tissue  are multiple fragments of skin measuring in aggregate 12 x 6 x 1cm  One of the fragments contains scar measuring 9 x  2cm  Representative sections are submitted in K through M  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast excess tissue  are multiple fragments of breast tissue with skin ellipses measuring in aggregate 16 x 12 x 5cm and weighing 400 grams  Representative sections are submitted in N through W  Resident  IVANA DELALLE  MD  PHD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Anne