Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 99 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 19 37 CLINICAL DATA  A 46 year old female with left breast cancer at two sites and positive lymph nodes                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  TWO HEALING BIOPSY CAVITIES  NO RESIDUAL CARCINOMA IS IDENTIFIED  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   REGIONAL DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 10 OF 10 NODES  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 18 03                                                                                     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     NOTE  At the request of Dr  Barbara Smith  who was concerned about a clinically suspicious axillary lymph node  this case was further evaluated  The gross specimen was re examined and additional sections of the largest nodes submitted in M P  In addition  multiple deeper levels were examined for the sections with the largest nodes  J M N O   Several nodes measure about 1 5cm in greatest dimension  The largest  2 0cm   is mostly replaced by fat  Most of the others show follicular hyperplasia and sinus histiocytosis  No tumor cells are identified  Added by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 19 03 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labelled with the patient s name and unit number and  left breast with axillary contents   is yellow breast tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm with REMOVED_DATE x 10 0cm skin ellipse  oriented with a short stitch delineating the superior margin and a long stitch delineating the lateral margin  The nipple and skin are unremarkable  There is a 3 5cm healed skin scar present 1 0cm medial to the nipple  The specimen is inked in black and sectioned to reveal a large excisional cavity  7 0cm in its largest dimension  present 4 0cm from the medial margin  7 0cm from the lateral margin  1 0cm to the superior margin  2 0cm to the inferior margin  and 3 0cm from the deep margin  On the surface of the cavity are several yellow pink nodules  probably consistent with previous biopsy  Further sectioning reveals another REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm  yellow pink  firm  rubbery mass present 3 0cm lateral to the biopsy cavity and 9 0cm to the lateral margin  3 0cm to the superior and inferior margins  and 4 0cm to the anterior and deep margins  Representative tissues are submitted in Cassettes A I  Section Code  A B  Superior and lateral wall of excision cavity  C  Anterior side of cavity wall  D  Grossly normal deep medial margin of the cavity  E  Fibrotic mass  F  Fibrotic mass at its deep margin  G  Additional tissues from fibrotic mass  H  Medial margin  I  Lateral margin and one lymph node of REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  present  0 2cm from the lateral margin  K  Two pieces of 2cm lymph nodes Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labelled with the patient s name and unit number and  axillary contents   is an aggregate of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  fatty  lymphoid tissue dissected the identified lymph node submitted in Cassette L  Resident  MANCONG ZHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  OR ROOM UNKNOWN REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  AXILLARY CONTENTS  LEFT  DISSECTION   report_end  , Positive.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 36 CLINICAL DATA  66 year old female with extensive fungating right breast mass  also history of Crohn s disease with ascites                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     COLON  RESECTION  SEVERELY ACTIVE CHRONIC GRANULOMATOUS COLITIS  CONSISTENT WITH CROHN S COLITIS  WITH ULCERATION  FISTULA FORMATION  AND MULTIFOCAL TRANSMURAL NECROSIS   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The distal margin shows severely active colitis with ulceration  The proximal margin shows fibrosis and regressed Peyer s patches  There is no evidence of dysplasia  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSIES  INFILTRATING ADENOCARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 57 Staff Pathologist  Fiona M  Graeme Cook  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 07 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  colon   is an ileocolonic resection specimen  82 0cm in length with an attached REMOVED_DATE x 10 0cm omentum and a 4 5cm length of distal ileum measuring 3 5cm in circumference proximally and 6 0cm in circumference distally  The serosal surface along the entire length of bowel is tan to brown and covered by indurated tan brown  hemorrhagic mesenteric fat  which creeps along the serosal surface in multiple areas and focally encases the segment of bowel  Approximately 21 0cm from the distal resection margin are two serosal defects  measuring 1 5cm in greatest dimension  surrounded by indurated hemorrhagic fat and lined by tan to brown fibrinous exudate  The surgeon states that multiple colonic perforations are present  now walled off by mesenteric fat  The segment of omentum is indurated  dark red to brown with a micronodular appearance  The segment of bowel is opened to reveal multiple regions where the mucosa is ulcerated  now lined by a tan to brown  focally green fibrinous exudate  surrounded by more preserved areas of mucosa resembling pseudopolyps  Towards the distal end of the specimen  the mucosa has a cobblestone appearance which extends to the distal resection margin  The region of the cecum and proximal ascending colon as well as the proximal resection margin appear spared of disease  In the region of ulcerative mucosa  the bowel wall appears markedly thickened measuring 1 2cm in maximal thickness  The more preserved areas of mucosa are sectioned to reveal a maximal thickness measuring 0 5cm  No appendix is identified  SEction Code  A  proximal resection margin B  distal resection margin C E  representative sections of serosal perforations surrounded by an indurated mesenteric fat F T  representative sections of diseased mucosa with cassettes  P  through  T  demonstrating the more cobblestone mucosa towards the distal end of the colon U  representative section of more normal appearing colonic mucosa V  representative section of indurated micronodular attached omentum  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast biopsy   are multiple tan yellow soft tissue cores  measuring 1 0cm in length and 0 2cm in diameter  submitted entirely in cassette W  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  Bernard Ralph Aserkoff  M D  PART A  COLON PART B  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSIES   report_end  , Positive.
