 receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 20 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast biopsy  is a breast biopsy specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 1cm tan white  firm nodule within 0 1cm of the closest surgical margin  The area with the stitch is inked red  over black   Representative section is frozen as FX  1 and kept frozen  Remainder in A D where the A section corresponds to the stitched area  ERPR done  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING AND IN SITU DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Asif Rashid  MD O R  Consulting Pathologist s   Anthony Mattia  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Hugh Auchincloss Jr   M D  Leslie Shu Tung Fang  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY   report_end  , Negative.
