Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 49 CLINICAL DATA  Bilateral breast cancer by fine needle aspirate                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY  SCANT BREAST PARENCHYMA WITH DISTORTED CYST LIKE STRUCTURE CONTAINING A DISLODGED FRAGMENT OF SLIGHTLY ATYPICAL EPITHELIAL CELLS  AND REACTIVE FIBROSIS   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The nature of the core biopsy specimen precludes definitive diagnosis  Multiple levels examined  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 27                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 51 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin in 2 separately labeled containers  Labeled  right   are 3  soft  tan pink cores of tissue ranging in size from a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  The specimen is submitted entirely in Cassette A  Labeled  left breast   are 3 ranging in size from a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm  The specimen is submitted entirely in Cassette B  Gross Description by  Jason Corbin Resident  SAMANTHA J  PULLIAM  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY   report_end  , Positive.
