cinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 19 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fragment of breast tissue with localizing wire  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm firm stellate nodule abutting the resection margin  Submitted entirely in cassettes A through I  with suspicious lesion in G and H  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST LESION  LESION GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Positive.
