Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 18 08 CLINICAL DATA  Fine needle aspiration was positive for malignant cells                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  70    REMOVED_DATE CM  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  WITH INVOLVEMENT OF BOTH SUPERFICIAL AND DEEP RESECTION MARGINS  SEE NOTE  2  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  30    CRIBRIFORM AND MICROPAPILLARY TYPES  WITH FOCAL COMEDO TYPE NECROSIS  EXTENDING TO INKED RESECTION MARGINS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  No definite lymphatic or blood vessel invasion is identified  The in situ component is largely confined to the region of infiltrating tumor  however  a wide margin is not present to assess for its presence away from the main tumor mass  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 21 23                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 34 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Labeled with the patient s name and unit number and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm fragment of breast tissue with a suture designating the deep margin  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a 1 0cm  hard  gritty  white area abutting the inked margin on the superficial aspect  A representative section of the lesion and the superficial margin is frozen as FX 1  now A  The deepest resection margin is designated blue  Representative sections of the remainder are submitted in B through F  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Essam Ahmed  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   report_end  , Positive.
