Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel  617  REMOVED_DATE    Surgical Pathology Report      Accession     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  J  MD  DOB  REMOVED_DATE  Age  40   Sex  F  MRN   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Location  PAC  Institution  MGH  Date of Operation  REMOVED_DATE  Date of Accession  REMOVED_DATE  Reported  REMOVED_DATE 15 55  Results To   Barbara Lynn Smith MD  PhD  William Gerald Austen MD    FINAL PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS   A  SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION  RIGHT AXILLA HOT AND BLUE  REMOVED_CASE_ID  289   No evidence of carcinoma in six lymph nodes  0 6    No evidence of treatment effect seen   The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed     Note  Immunostained slides for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2  cytokeratin 7  and  pankeratin were examined on tissue levels from each of 3 blocks       B  SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION  LEFT AXILLA  728   No evidence of carcinoma in one lymph node  0 1    The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed     Note  Immunostained slides for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2  cytokeratin 7  and  pankeratin were examined on tissue levels from each of 2 blocks       C  SUBAREOLAR NIPPLE MARGIN  LEFT BREAST   There is no evidence of malignancy       D  BREAST TISSUE EXCISION  LEFT ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR AND SUPERIOR   There is no evidence of malignancy       E  PORT A CATH REMOVAL  LEFT CHEST   Gross only examination  see gross description        F  BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY NIPPLE SPARING  LEFT   There is no evidence of malignancy       G  BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY NIPPLE SPARING  RIGHT   No residual carcinoma identified   Healing biopsy sites   No evidence of carcinoma in one axillary lymph node by H E staining  0 1   no  treatment effect identified     Note  The patient presented with a palpable mass in the right breast  which on  mammography and ultrasound dated REMOVED_DATE corresponded to a 1 2cm mass  No  abnormal lymph nodes were noted by imaging  The patient received pre operative  neoadjuvant chemotherapy  Upon completion  clinical exam on REMOVED_DATE showed no  palpable masses in either breast and the patient was considered to have had an   excellent clinical response  to chemotherapy  No breast imaging information is  available post completion of chemotherapy  She then underwent bilateral  mastectomies with sentinel lymph node biopsies   Gross exam of the right mastectomy specimen showed a mass at the 12 o clock  position measuring up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm  Histologic examination of this  mass shows healing biopsy sites and an area of fibroadenomatous change measuring  up to 1 7cm on glass slides  Scattered foci of macrophage collections  chronic  inflammation  stromal edema  and hemosiderin deposition are seen  these changes  are not completely specific and could be related to either biopsy site changes  or effects of chemotherapy  No residual carcinoma is identified in the right  breast  Histologic exam of the right axillary and sentinel lymph nodes also  show no evidence of carcinoma or treatment effect   The patient is considered to have had a Pathologic Complete Response  The  findings here would correspond to a residual cancer burden score of 0 and Miller  Payne grade 5  of 5        H  SUBAREOLAR NIPPLE MARGIN  RIGHT BREAST   There is no evidence of malignancy       I  BREAST MARGIN  RIGHT ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR   There is no evidence of malignancy        Electronically Signed Out By Amy Ly MD       Resident Pathologist   Jonathan H Chen MD  PhD      By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis  certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or  corrected the diagnosis       INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   1A   SENTINEL NODE RIGHT AXILLA    Small eosinophilic focus in one of five lymph nodes    histi