Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  19 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  19 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 05 CLINICAL DATA  79 year old with invasive ductal carcinoma by FNA                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM FOCALLY SHOWING EXTENSIVE MUCIN PRODUCTION  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  FORMING ONE NODULE REMOVED_DATE CM AND SEVERAL OTHER TINY NODULES AND INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 11 OF 11 OF LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 32                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT  NODULE  1  DUCTAL CARCINOMA    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  BREAST  LEFT  NODULE  2  LOBULAR CARCINOMA    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 07 38 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast with axillary contents  is a 17 x 15 x 4 8cm portion of left breast tissue with 15 x 4 x 0 8cm axillary content  and an 18 x 7cm overlying skin ellipse which has a double black suture denoting the superior resection margin  The nipple is located 1 5cm from the inferior skin margin and 3 7cm from the superior skin margin  which is retracted and surrounded by hemorrhagic polypoid mass  It measures approximately 2cm in greatest diameter including the surrounding lesions  An approximately 2cm in greatest dimension ecchymosis is present between the nipple and the superior skin resection margin  The remaining skin surface is unremarkable  No nodule is identified upon palpation  It is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm stellate  firm  pink tan lesion underneath the nipple  approximately 0 2cm from the skin  1 8cm from the inferior resection margin  and 0 8cm from the deep resection margin  A separate additional pink tan and firm nodule  REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 8cm is identified approximately 6cm from the lateral margin  4 5cm from the superior margin and 0 5cm from the deep resection margin  The remainder of the specimen is composed of yellow adipose tissue admixed with unremarkable breast parenchyma  No gross necrosis is identified  The axillary contents consists predominantly of soft  yellow tan adipose tissue without identifiable nodule  SECTION CODE A C  Nipple and adjacent lesions  D F  Nodule  1  G I  Nodule  2  J K  Deep resection margin  L M  Random  N P  Lymph node  Resident  HENRY DONG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Positive.
