Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 20 CLINICAL DATA  Mass on mammography                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE II III  REMOVED_DATE CM  90   EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE INKED MARGINS  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBIFORM TYPE  10   CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS  PRESENT IN 7 OF 8 SLIDES  NOTE  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  The gross diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 17 35 Staff Pathologist  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent 