d for lymph nodes and no lymph nodes are grossly appreciated  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections  calcified scar  located between 1 and 3 o clock in the outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire biopsy cavity located between 6 and 7 o clock   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  breast parenchyma intervening the scar and the biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  breast parenchyma  inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  breast parenchyma  outer quadrant  Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 26   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 05 06 51PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  Amendment  1 by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on Thursday February 05   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 11 07 52AM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The invasive tumor cells and the adjacent ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells  grade 1  stain for estrogen receptor protein  See note  Note  The sections stained for progesterone receptor protein and HER 2 c erbB 2 do not show the invasive tumor cells or the adjacent ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells  grade 1   The second focus of ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells  grade 3  do not stain for estrogen and progesterone receptor proteins  and HER 2 c erbB 2  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor ce