ntified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  The distances to all margins measures 0 2cm or greater  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS   2 SUMMARY OF AXILLARY LYMPH NODES TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  1 TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  16 Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   1 Extracapsular extension  None  Other forms of axillary involvement  None  Note  Due to an issue with fixation and tissue processing in this case  the histologic findings and immunohistochemical staining results are limited  A panel of immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin  p63  myosin and calponin were performed on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The immunostaining pattern is limited due to sectioning artifact and lack of staining in several sections  however  the myoepithelial layer is highlighted in a few areas of the radial scar and supports the diagnosis  Similarly  immunostains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2  cytokeratin 7  and pankeratin on nine tissue levels of the sentinel lymph node  part C  failed to show appropriate staining and are interpreted as non contributory  The diagnosis of metastatic ductal carcinoma is based on the H E stained sections  Dr  Fritz Koerner and Dr  David Wilbur have reviewed the slides for part A and concur with the diagnosis of radial scar  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast needle biopsy   is a 6 x 4 x 2 5cm oriented breast tissue with a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral and localization wire in place  The long axis of the specimen is going from medial to lateral and the specimen is inked as follows  Anterior  Blue  Posterior  Black  Superior  Green  and Inferior  Yellow 