ure below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan pink lymph node with attached tan yellow adipose tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted for frozen section as FX 1  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   right axillary non sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm irregular portion of glistening yellow lobulated lymph node bearing adipose tissue  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm well circumscribed rubbery tan pink possible lymph node is identified  The lymph node is trisected and submitted in entirety labeled  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x 16 x 3 2cm right simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch designating 12 o clock  The specimen is partially surfaced by a 24 x 8 5cm elliptical portion of wrinkled tan skin  which contains a REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm well healed scar and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm unremarkable nipple  The anterior margin is inked blue  the posterior black  and the specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm hemorrhagic defect located in the mid inferior aspect of the specimen subjacent to the skin scar and coming within 0 5cm of the posterior margin  This defect is consistent with a previous biopsy site  The tissue surrounding the defect is dense rubbery tan white fibrous tissue with focal areas of hemorrhage and fat necrosis  No lesions or masses are identified  The remaining cut surfaces reveal multiple blue black nodules that are filled with red brown hemorrhagic substa