Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 54 CLINICAL DATA  Left nodule on routine mammography                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED    95    WITH FOCAL CANCERIZATION OF LOBULES   5    THE TUMOR FOCALLY IS PRESENT WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF AN INKED MARGIN OF RESECTION  A SEPARATE FOCUS OF ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA IS IDENTIFIED  NOTE  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is identified  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 18 24                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  11 MAY 95 at 14 37 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm portion of tan to yellow fibroadipose tissue  with a localizing wire in place  A roentgenogram accompanies the specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a yellow cut surface with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm white firm nodule  less than 0 1cm from the closest inked margin  A representative section of the nodule is frozen as frozen section  1  now A  and the remaining nodule submitted entirely in B  The remaining fibroadipose tissue is submitted entirely in C through K  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST LEFT  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  SCOTT D  URBAN  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  Max L  Goodman  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY   report_end  , Positive.
