 staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 59 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm fragment of breast with a localizing wire in place and an accompanying x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 9cm  white  stellate firm nodule located adjacent to an inked resection margin  All fibrous tissue is submitted in A through J  with the suspicious nodule in A through D  remaining non  suspicious fatty tissue   1 0 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm   is not submitted  No other masses are seen    Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA BUT TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  David William Rattner  M D  Diane Elise Rich  M D  PART   BREAST TISSUE  LEFT    report_end  , Positive.
