Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  15 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  15 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 24 CLINICAL DATA  Abnormal mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  2   FORMING A NODULE REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION IN TISSUE SECTION AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  COMEDO TYPE  INVOLVING NINE OF TEN SECTIONS  EXTENDING TO THE MARGINS OF THE SPECIMEN  AND HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 58                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 AUG 94 at 07 26 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x 4 x 1 5cm excision biopsy of fibrofatty tissue with ill defined  rubbery nodularity  REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 5cm adjacent to inked resection margin and corresponding to mammographic abnormality  Representative sections in cassettes A through J  with suspicious area in A through I  Resident  Ajit J  Alles  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  CARCINOMA  PROBABLY INTRADUCTAL  O R  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   LEFT BREAST  BIOPSY   report_end  , Negative.
