Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  04 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  04 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 42 CLINICAL DATA  70 year old female with a history of infiltrating ductal carcinoma of the right breast who now presents for a re excision and axillary node dissection                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM TYPES  FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION  FIBROSIS  CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  FAT NECROSIS  AND HEMORRHAGE CONSISTENT WITH BIOPSY CAVITY  FIBROADENOMAS  3  0 5 CM  AND MICROSCOPIC   INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 11 OF 11 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The residual tumor is multifocal with the largest focus measuring 0 2cm  on the slide  The tumor extends to 0 3cm  of the arbitrarily designated superior margin and focally extends to another inked resection margin  There is no infiltrating carcinoma present  No venous or lymphatic invasion is identified  The lymph nodes are very small  less than 0 1cm  to 0 3cm    and they and the surrounding axillary fat are negative for neoplasm  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 03                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number  in two separate parts  Labeled  A  re excision  is a 54 gram  9 x REMOVED_DATE x 3cm   unoriented  breast re excision specimen  with an overlying 9 x 2cm  skin ellipse  The epidermal surface of the skin ellipse is notable for an eccentrically placed  7cm  long  well healed scar  located 0 7cm  from one edge and 1 2cm  from the other edge  The specimen is arbitrarily oriented so that the scar is located closest to the superior margin  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1cm   tan white  firm  stellate lesion with a central REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  cystic and hemorrhagic cavity  extends to the skin surface  anterior margin  and focally to the superior and inferior margins  and is located 1 5cm  from the medial margin  2 5cm  from the lateral margin  and 0 5cm  from the deep margin  In addition  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm   white  round  ovoid  rubbery  firm area separate from the main mass  located 0 2cm  from the deep margin  0 2cm  from the superior margin  1 8cm  from the inferior margin  1 2cm  from the anterior margin  2cm  from the medial margin  and 3 5cm  from the lateral margin  There is a third lesion  that is round  white  and papillary  measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm   and located subadjacent to the superior resection margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is yellow  soft  lobulated  and interspersed with thin  white  rubbery  shiny fibrous bands  Labeled  B  axilla  is a 8 x 6 x 1 5cm  portion of fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is dissected to reveal multiple lymph nodes  ranging in size from less than 0 1cm  to 0 3cm  greatest dimension  Each lymph node is submitted entirely  The remaining fibroadipose tissue is also entirely submitted  Section code  A Medial margin  en face  B Lateral margin  en face  C Inferior margin  radial section  D Superior margin  radial section  E Deep margin  radial section  F Anterior margin  skin with tumor  radial section  G H Rubbery nodule  I Papillary nodule  J L Biopsy cavity  entirely  N Q Breast parenchyma surrounding biopsy cavity  representative sections  R S Breast parenchyma  representative sections  T Y Axillary lymph nodes  Z AN Axillary fibroadipose tissue  entirely  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Ashby Carter Moncure  M D  PART