Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  ACCESSIONED ON  15 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 02 CLINICAL DATA  Pre Op Diagnosis  Abnormal mammogram  Post Op Diagnosis  Pending pathology  Surgical procedure  Exc  Lt  Breast Bx  w needle loc   surg Proc cont                                                                                       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 18 42                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 35                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTSIDE LOCATION REPORTS TO  Rebecca Ann Osgood  M D  OUTSIDE INSTITUTION  THE CAMBRIDGE HOSPITAL OUTSIDE PATHOLOGIST  Rebecca Osgood  M D  DEPT  OF PATH  CAMBRIDGE HOSPITAL  REMOVED_CASE_ID  CAMBRIDGE ST  CAMBRIDGE  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PART   BREAST  LEFT   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Date of Procedure  06 MAR  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Slides  2 Blocks  1   report_end  , Positive.
