Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 10 44 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  NEEDLE BIOPSY   INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  grade 2  measuring 2 4cm in greatest dimension in tissue section and extending to the margins of the specimen in several regions  SEE NOTE  BREAST  RIGHT   NEW SUPERIOR MARGIN    THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 3 OF 3 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Invasion of blood vessels or lymphatic vessels is not seen  The tumor would be expected to contain estrogen receptors  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 22                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 10 37                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTSIDE LOCATION REPORTS TO  Simon Powell  M D  OUTSIDE INSTITUTION  MOUNT AUBURN HOSPITAL OUTSIDE PATHOLOGIST  Gregory P  Gauvin  MD PATHOLOGY DEPT   MT  AUBURN HOSPITAL 330 MT  AUBURN STREET CAMBRIDGE  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PART A  RIGHT BREAST NEEDLE BIOPSY   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Date of Procedure  28 JAN  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Slides  2 Blocks  0 PART B  RIGHT BREAST EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Date of Procedure  09 MAR  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Slides  8 Blocks  1 PART C  RIGHT BREAST   NEW SUPERIOR MARGIN     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Date of Procedure  09 MAR  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Slides  1 Blocks  0 PART D  RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Date of Procedure  09 MAR  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Slides  3 Blocks  0   report_end  , Positive.
