Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  25 MAY 93 ACCESSIONED ON  25 MAY 93 at 10 04 CLINICAL DATA  Patient has a history of bilateral breast carcinoma  status post radiation 18 years ago  Patient is status post left mastectomy for angiosarcoma  Now she has a new nodule on the right breast which is clinically angiosarcoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY  ANGIOSARCOMA GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The angiosarcoma is located within the reticular dermis of the skin and extends along fibrous septae into the superficial breast parenchyma  The resection margins are free of tumor  The breast parenchyma away from the angiosarcoma shows marked atrophy  focal fibrosis and no evidence of malignancy  The skin and deep surgical resection margins are free of tumor  The skin of the breast exhibits dermal fibrosis and focal ectatic superficially located lymphatics  BREAST  RIGHT  SEPARATELY SUBMITTED  RESECTION  ATROPHY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   RESECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 11 LYMPH NODES  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  FROZEN SECTION  1   FIBROFATTY TISSUE WITH FOCAL IRREGULAR SHAPED BLOOD VESSELS  DEFINITIVE ANGIOSARCOMA IS NOT IDENTIFIED  Diagnosis by  John O Connell  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 10                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab is a 29 x 13 x 5cm right modified radical mastectomy specimen  Skin covers the entire anterior surface  The nipple is 1cm in diameter and non retracted  No scars are noted on the epidermal surface  A 0 5cm in diameter blue nodule is present in the skin of the lower outer  lower axillary  region  3cm from the nearest skin resection margin  On cutting  the nodule is blood filled  and collapses to reveal an ill defined red tan fibrous band 0 3cm thick in the superficial dermis  The underlying breast parenchyma appears uninvolved  Elsewhere  the skin overlying the breast is indurated and displays patchy areas of blue red discoloration  Sectioning through these areas reveals epidermal superficial dermal red discoloration  Sectioning through the underlying breast reveals yellow parenchyma that is focally firm and fibrotic  No discrete masses are identified  Section Code  A  nipple  B E  blue nodule in toto  F  underlying breast  hemorrhagic  G J  areas of blue red skin discoloration  K R  representative breast from lateral to medial  FF  skin at resection margin nearest to tumor  GG  breast at deep inked margin nearest to tumor  Received separately  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  Right breast  is a 14 x 5 x 3cm fragment of breast which is sectioned to reveal fibrofatty parenchyma  Focal punctate areas of hemorrhage are present peripherally  No masses are identified representative tissue in casettes S through Z  Received separately  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  Right axillary nodes  is a 9 x 5 x 3cm fragment of adipose tissue which is dissected to reveal several firm  tan pink nodules 1cm in greatest dimension  Representative of each is submitted in cassettes AA through CC  Received separately in the frozen section lab  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  Right breast biopsy  is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 3cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue which is inked and bisected to reveal a tan white cut surface  Representative is frozen as frozen section  1  Frozen section  1 is submitted in cassette DD and the remaining non frozen tissue is submitted in EE  Resident  Andrea Flieder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY   DENSE FIBROSIS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O 