Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Cytology  Cytology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel  617  REMOVED_DATE    Non Gyn Cytology Report        Accession     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME   DOB  REMOVED_DATE  Age  72   Sex  F  MRN   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Institution  MGH  Location  WRN 219  PATH FINE NEEDLE  Date of Collection  REMOVED_DATE  Date of Accession  REMOVED_DATE  Reported  REMOVED_DATE 18 14  Results to   Kevin S  Hughes MD        FINAL DIAGNOSIS    A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT LATERAL  1     SPECIMEN ADEQUACY   Satisfactory for evaluation     INTERPRETATION   POSITIVE FOR MALIGNANT CELLS     DIAGNOSIS   Malignant neoplasm  suggestive of angiosarcoma  See note accompanying cell  block       B  BREAST CELLBLOCK  LEFT LATERAL  1     SPECIMEN ADEQUACY   Evaluation limited by scant cellularity     INTERPRETATION   POSITIVE FOR MALIGNANT CELLS     DIAGNOSIS   Malignant neoplasm  rare cells  suggestive of angiosarcoma  See note     NOTE  The cytological smears from the left lateral and left medial locations  show identical features  Both are cellular  and composed of dyshesive  mostly  singly dispersed cells that are mostly spindle shaped  with occasional  epithelioid forms  The cells have delicate cytoplasm with tapered extensions   and the nuclei are pleomorphic and hyperchromatic  with coarsely clumped  chromatin  and mitotic activity  A tiny group of these same cells are  identified within the cell block preparation  Using immunoperoxidase methods on  deeper levels of this block  most of the neoplastic cells express  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   no  staining is identified for cytokeratin or factor VIII related antigen in  sparsely cellular levels  Together with the cytomorphological features and  clinical observations  the findings are suggestive of mammary angiosarcoma       C  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT MEDIAL  2     SPECIMEN ADEQUACY   Satisfactory for evaluation     INTERPRETATION   POSITIVE FOR MALIGNANT CELLS     DIAGNOSIS   Malignant neoplasm  suggestive of angiosarcoma  See note accompnying cell  block       D  BREAST CELLBLOCK  LEFT MEDIAL  2     SPECIMEN ADEQUACY   Unsatisfactory for evaluation  Specimen processed and examined  but  insufficiently cellular     INTERPRETATION   INSUFFICIENT CELLULAR MATERIAL FOR DIAGNOSIS     DIAGNOSIS   Virtually acellular specimen         Electronically Signed Out By   John Henry Eichhorn MD  Ronald N  Arpin  SCT      RAPID INTERPRETATION  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT LATERAL  1   FNA Rapid Interpretation     Malignant  suspect angiosarcoma     Pathologist  Elena F  Brachtel  M D         C  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT MEDIAL  2   FNA Rapid Interpretation     Malignant  suspect angiosarcoma     Pathologist  Elena F  Brachtel  M D       PROCEDURES ADDENDA  Patient Evaluation and Management  with Interpretation     PATIENT EVALUATION    Chief Complaint  This 73 year old female was referred to the fine needle  aspiration clinic by Dr  K  Hughes for consultation and diagnosis of red raised  papules in the left breast     Clinical History  S P breast cancer  New multiple papules left breast  REMOVED_DATE    0 8cm     Review of Symptoms   Constitutional  NAD    Allergy to lidocaine latex  Not known   Medications anticoagulants  See clinical notes     Review of Patient Data   Radiology  REMOVED_DATE XR chest wall no evidence of rib fractures  Past Histology   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Left breast excision  IDC  1 2cm  Grade REMOVED_DATE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Office notes  REMOVED_DATE Dr S Sweetnam    Physical Examination  Laterality was established according to departmental  protocol  Examination of the left breast reveals several raised papules REMOVED_DATE 6  cm in the inferior breast  The entire left breast is tender and shows  hematoma like discoloration  Well healed horizontal scar is present at 12 00h  2  cm from areola     Assessment  Based on the clinical history and physical examination  an FNAB is  warranted of the lateral nodule   1   and of the most medial of the nodules    2      Procedure  The procedure and complications were explained to the patient and  consent was obtained   Site  1  2 aspirates were performed of the lateral nodule   1  using 23 gauge  needles without anesthesia and without complications  2 slides were stained for  immediate evaluation  additional tissue was submitted for further evaluation   Site  2  2 aspirates were performed of the medial nodule   2  using 23 gauge  needles without anesthesia and without complications  1 slide was stained for  immediate evaluation  additional tissue was submitted for further evaluation     Disposition  The immediate interpretation findings were not discussed with the  patient  The preliminary results were communicated to Dr  Hughes in person at 4  o clock p m          Electronically Signed Out By  Elena F  Brachtel MD on REMOVED_DATE 14 22       CLINICAL HISTORY    Status post breast cancer left  New raided red papules 0 4 0 6cm left breast         SPECIMEN SOURCE  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT LATERAL  1  B  BREAST CELLBLOCK  LEFT LATERAL  1  C  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT MEDIAL  2  D  BREAST CELLBLOCK  LEFT MEDIAL  2    GROSS DESCRIPTION  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT LATERAL  1  Received 2 fixed and 2 air dried  slides     B  BREAST CELLBLOCK  LEFT LATERAL  1  Received in formalin  labeled with  patient name and medical number   REMOVED_CASE_ID    is a collodion bag  Entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      C  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT MEDIAL  2  Received 1 fixed and 1 air dried slides     D  BREAST CELLBLOCK  LEFT MEDIAL  2  Received in formalin  labeled with  patient name and medical number   REMOVED_CASE_ID    is a collodion bag  Entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID            Specimen  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT LATERAL  1  Specimen  BREAST CELLBLOCK  LEFT LATERAL  1  Specimen  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT MEDIAL  2  Specimen  BREAST CELLBLOCK  LEFT MEDIAL  2       report_end  , Positive.
