Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 09 45 CLINICAL DATA  Nodule in previous mastectomy site  Rule out recurrent breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT CHEST WALL   EXCISION  INFILTRATING AND IN SITU DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  Note  The infiltrating component comprises approximately 80  of the tumor mass  with the remainder being in situ  The infiltrating component is moderately to poorly differentiated  grade 2 3 3   The tumor is 2 0cm in greatest dimension  However  the margins are widely positive  and tumor invades skeletal muscle  Vascular invasion is not identified  Scattered benign breast parenchymal elements are present  Dr  A  Rosenberg has reviewed selected slides and concurs with the diagnosis  Diagnosis by  Daniel Rubin  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 15                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS  LEFT CHEST WALL   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 20 GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name unit number  and  Left chest wall lesion   and is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  tan  firm piece of tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a tan white  gritty area  Representative sections are frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  The remainder of the tissue is submitted entirely in A through C  Resident  Jo Ann E  Haney  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 LEFT CHAST WALL LESIONP   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA IN SKELETAL MUSCLE  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Essam Ahmed  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  PART   LEFT CHEST WALL LESION   report_end  , Negative.
