taining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 55 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast mass  are two fragments of breast tissue  The first measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm  it is inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibroadipose tissue without specific lesions  It is submitted entirely in cassette I through L  The second measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm  and is remarkable for a stellate retracted hard  scirrous area  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 2cm stellate hard white to tan nodule grossly involving the resection margin  A representative section of the nodule is frozen as frozen section  1  and kept frozen for Cox 5  The main nodule is submitted in cassette A through D and the remainder of this portion of tissue is submitted in cassette E through H  Received fresh in two separate parts  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and as follows  The first container labeled  Endocervical curettings  and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 0 3cm aggregate of soft  tan pink fragments of tissue  with a small amount of mucoid material admixed within  The specimen is wrapped and submitted entirely as M  The second container  labeled  Endometrial curettings  consists of a 2 x 1 x 0 3cm aggregate of red brown minute fragments of soft tissue  which are submitted entirely as N  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE D