Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated  Type  Cytology  Cytology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel  617  REMOVED_DATE    GYN Cytology Report        Accession     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  M   DOB  REMOVED_DATE  Age  54   Sex  F  MRN   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Institution  MGH  Location  CHELSEA 151 ADULT MED  FL 2  Date of Collection  REMOVED_DATE  Date of Accession  REMOVED_DATE  Reported  REMOVED_DATE 12 48  Results to   Lauriane P O Leary NP        FINAL DIAGNOSIS    A  CERVICAL  LIQUID BASED SPECIMEN     SPECIMEN ADEQUACY   Satisfactory for evaluation     INTERPRETATION   NEGATIVE FOR INTRAEPITHELIAL LESION OR MALIGNANCY     ADDITIONAL INFORMATION   A manual review was performed for Quality Control purposes   This specimen was prescreened using the BD FocalPoint GS Imaging System         Electronically Signed Out By  Mary Rego  CT ASCP     Diane Kuebler  CT ASCP     Cervical cytology is a screening test primarily for squamous cancers and  precursors and has associated false negative and false positive results  New  technologies such as liquid based preparations may decrease but will not  eliminate all false negative results  Regular sampling and follow up of  unexplained clinical signs and symptoms are recommended to minimize false  negative results         PROCEDURES ADDENDA  HPV Testing  Requested     HPV Test    Negative for human papillomavirus types 16  18 and the  Other high risk  probe  set  Includes 31  33  35  39  45  52  56  59  66  68  by Roche cobase  REMOVED_CASE_ID   HR HPV analysis     Clinical correlation is advised  The accuracy and precision of this test has  been verified in the Cytopathology laboratory of the Massachusetts General  Hospital  This test has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug  Administration  FDA             Electronically Signed Out By  Melissa Ring  CT ASCP  on REMOVED_DATE 12 21       CLINICAL HISTORY  Date