Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 31 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MALIGNANT SPINDLE CELL NEOPLASM  high grade  3 3   INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  comedo type  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The spindle cell neoplasm grows in a storiform pattern and produces neoplastic osteoid  If pathologists encountered such a tumor in most other settings  they would make the diagnosis of osteosarcoma  In this case  however  the cytological similarities beyween the intraductal carcinoma and the sarcomatous component would lead many observers to interpret the invasive cells as a sarcomatoid carcinoma  The distinction between a sarcoma and a sarcomatoid carcinoma cannot be made with confidence on the basis of these three sections and in the absence of special studies  furthermore  such a distinction might not have clinical relevance  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 09 11                                                                                                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTSIDE LOCATION REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  Simon Powell  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  OUTSIDE INSTITUTION  JOHNSON MEMORIAL HOSPITAL PART   LEFT BREAST MASS   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Date of Procedure  26 JAN  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Slides  3 Blocks  0   report_end  , Negative.
