 Wild Type    PTEN  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    388C Wild Type  PTEN  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    517C Wild Type  PTEN  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    697C Wild Type  PTEN  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID fs   800delA Wild Type     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    524G Wild Type   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    733G Wild Type   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    742C Wild Type   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    743G Wild Type   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    817C Wild Type   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    818G Wild Type   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    916C Wild Type      INTERPRETATION   POSITIVE FOR  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  MUTATION   This test does not rule out mutations in one of the assayed genes which might  occur at a low prevalence     TEST INFORMATION   We have developed a multiplexed allele specific assay to detect somatic  mutations in tumor DNA extracted from formalin fixed paraffin embedded samples   The assay SNaPshot Version 2 detects mutations in 60 different loci from 14  cancer genes  Briefly  multiplex PCR using tumor DNA is followed by mutation  detection using single base extension sequencing technology  SNaPshot  Applied  Biosystems   In addition  a separate multiplex PCR reaction using primers  flanking EGFR exon 19  EGFR exon 20 and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  exon 20 are used to detect  in frame activating insertions or deletions in EGFR and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  that may not be  detected using SNaPshot  The mutations are visualized using an ABI  REMOVED_CASE_ID  DNA  analyzer  The average analytic sensitivity of detecting mutations in this assay  has been established in our laboratory at approximately 5  mutant allele     This test was developed  and its performance characteristics were determined by  the MGH Diagnostic Molecular Pathology Laboratory  It has not been approved by  the U S  food and Drug Administration  The FDA has determined that such  clearance or approval is not necessary  This test is used for clinical  purposes  Pursuant to the requirements of CLIA 88  this laboratory has  established and verified the test accuracy and precision     Question concerning these values should be addressed to Dr  A  John Iafrate at   617 726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   MGH internal address  MGH Diagnostic Molecular Pathology  Laboratory  Massachusetts General Hospital  70 Blossom Street  GRJ  REMOVED_CASE_ID    Boston  MA   REMOVED_CASE_ID          Final Diagnosis by Anthony J Iafrate M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on  Friday REMOVED_MONTH 03   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 04 26 05PM  By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final  Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed  or corrected the diagnoses     PART   Fixed Tissue Block  MS 10  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    SNAPSHOT       report_end  , Positive.
