ED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm indurated  gray white mass  which abuts the anterior margin and extends to 0 6cm from the posterior margin  1 3cm from the lateral margin  0 7cm from the superior margin  and 1 7cm from the inferior margin  The specimen is entirely submitted from superior to inferior in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  with the superior margin radially sectioned in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   the inferior margin radially sectioned in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and the entire lesion in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON    1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  Some tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  Focally  the tumor cells show moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administra