Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 16 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   12 O CLOCK    CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  BREAST  LEFT   UPPER INNER    CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 51                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   12 O CLOCK     The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  BREAST  LEFT   UPPER INNER    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 06 57 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are four soft  tan to tan brown cores of tissue  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  submitted entirely in cassette A  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two tan brown cores of tissue  the smaller measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  submitted entirely in cassette B  Gross Description by  Jason Corbin Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Daniel Benjamin Kopans  M D  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST   12 O CLOCK   CORE BIOPSY PART B  LEFT BREAST   UPPER INNER   CORE BIOPSY   report_end  , Positive.
