Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  28 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 55 CLINICAL DATA  66 year old with right breast FNA positive for ductal carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  10    SEVERAL SEPARATE FOCI  EACH REMOVED_DATE   REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  GRADE 2  EXTENDING FOCALLY TO AN ANTEROLATERAL MARGIN  SECTION B   NEGATIVE FOR DEFINITE LYMPHATIC OR BLOOD VASCULAR INVASION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  90    COMEDO TYPE  HIGH GRADE  EXTENSIVELY PRESENT ON 6 OF 7 SECTIONS  SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM  SECTIONS B AND C   PRESENT AT AN ANTEROLATERAL MARGIN  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSES ARE CONFIRMED  BREAST  RIGHT   ADDITIONAL LATERAL MARGIN    BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  SEVERAL FOCI ON 4 OF 5 SECTIONS  UP TO REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  AT MARGINS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  5 OF 5 SECTIONS  BREAST  RIGHT   ADDITIONAL SHAVE MARGIN    BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SMALL FOCI  GRADE 2  AT A MARGIN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  BREAST  RIGHT   ADDITIONAL SUPERIOR MARGIN    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   REGIONAL NODE DISSECTION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 24 OF 32 NODES  WITHOUT EXTRANODAL EXTENSION  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 57                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 29     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Right   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 32 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  breast lump  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  There is a short stitch denoting the superior aspect  a long stitch denoting the lateral aspect  and short and long stitches denoting the deep margin  The entire specimen is inked black  the deep margin is overinked in blue  and the lateral margin is overinked in red  Sectioning reveals a 1cm in greatest dimension somewhat stellate and granular tan lesion abutting the anteriolateral margin approximately 3 0cm inferior to the superior margin  Additionally there is a 1 0cm in greatest dimension tan pink slightly firm nodule  located more inferiorly  which comes within 0 3cm of the lateral margin  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm irregular  slightly gritty white lesion which is located even more inferiorly and abuts the lateral margin grossly  Section code  A  FX 1  representative section of stellate lesion  B C  Remainder of stellate lesion  relative to anterolateral margin  D  Nodule relative to lateral margin  E F  Irregular white  gritty lesion  entirely submitted  relative to lateral margin  G  FX 2  tissue from inferior pole  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional lateral margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm irregular fragment of fibroadipose tissue  consisting of grossly unremarkable breast parenchyma  The specimen is entirely submitted in H L  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional shaved margin  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm aggregate of multiple pieces of fibroadipose tissue  No gross lesions are identified  The entire specimen is submitted in M R  Received fr