  stellate  tan white  indurated mass  which extends to 0 3cm from the superior margin  1 0cm from the anterior margin  0 5cm from the posterior margin  0 3cm from the inferior margin  2 0cm from the medial margin  and 2 3cm from the lateral margin  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral margin taken en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved parenchyma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire mass to closest anterior and superior margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial margin taken en face  Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  The tumor cell membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   over overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA