 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 47 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue  inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm firm  ill defined area that is 0 4cm from the inked resection margin  A representative section is frozen as FX  1  and saved frozen  The remainder of the tissue is submitted entirely in A D  Labeled  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm mastectomy specimen with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 11 0cm skin ellipse containing a 5 0cm sutured excision site and an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm axillary tail  The deep margin is inked  specimen is sectioned to reveal a biopsy site which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm in overall dimensions and comes to 1 0cm from the deep margin  closest margin   Section code  E  biopsy cavity and closest  deep  margin F H  representative sections of the biopsy cavity I J  representative sections of fibrotic area adjacent to the biopsy cavity K  unremarkable breast tissue away from the biopsy cavity L P  lymph nodes Resident  LISA A  GALLAGHER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  EXTENDING TO A MARGIN  O R  Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Ashby 