Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 MAY 95 ACCESSIONED ON  11 MAY 95 at 11 31 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  COLLOID  MUCINOUS  TYPE  SINGLE FOCUS REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST OVERALL DIMENSION  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Tumor comes within 0 05cm of an inked margin of the involved fragment  The other four specimens are negative for tumor  No invasion of lymphatics or vessels is noted  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  15 MAY 95 at 14 05                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 07 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  are five fragments of breast tissue  with an unattached localizing wire  and accompanying specimen radiograph  The largest two fragments measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  and the remaining three  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in aggregate  Sectioning reveals a 0 8cm nodule  abutting the inked margin in the first fragment  a representative section of which is frozen as frozen section  1 and submitted in A  The remainder of this fragment is submitted in B through E  with the nodule in B  The entirety of the remaining fragments are submitted entirely in F through S  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST  CARCINOMA  CONSISTENT WITH COLLOID TYPE  O R  Resident  Robin E  Kirby  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Andrew Louis Warshaw  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Positive.
