ined with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm breast biopsy containing a 0 9cm  gritty  stellate lesion approaching the inked resection margins  A small piece is frozen as FX  1 and saved frozen  Remainder of lesion submitted in A to B  The rest of the specimen in C F  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  BIOPSY  TUBULAR CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Positive.
