stration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 AUG 99 at 16 04 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Laboratory  labelled with the patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X 0 3cm  irregular  yellow tan  fibrofatty piece of tissue  which is bisected to reveal a white  homogeneous  cut surface  The specimen is frozen in its entirety as FX  1  now in A  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Laboratory  labelled with the patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X 1 5cm  yellow  fibrofatty piece of tissue with a short stitch superior and a long stitch lateral  The specimen is inked black and sectioned to reveal a white  firm  well circumscribed mass measuring REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X 1 4cm that abuts both the posterior deep margin and the inferior margin  it is 0 3cm from the superior margin  0 3cm from the anterior margin  0 5cm from the lateralmost margin  and 0 6cm from the medialmost margin  The superior margin is overinked in blue  the anterior margin is overinked in red  and the posterior inferior margin remains black  There is an ill defined  firm area measuring REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X 0 3cm in the lateralmost margin of the specimen and 0 3cm in the posterior deep margin  The specimen is submitted entirely after each individual slice is bisected in B through N  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and designated left breast final superior posterior margin is a fragment of fibrofatty tissue 2 x 1 x 0 5cm  The specimen is inked  serially sectioned and entirely submitted in O and P  No gross lesions are identified  Gross Description by  JOHN BISSONNETTE  MD Resident  VIKRAM DESHPANDE  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     LYMPH NO