Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 39 CLINICAL DATA  Infiltrating ductal carcinoma  REMOVED_CASE_ID   suspicious mammogram  REMOVED_CASE_ID   biopsy negative  now for right mastectomy and reduction mammoplasty of left breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY      BIOPSY CAVITY WITH FAT NECROSIS  FOAMY HISTIOCYTES  CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION TO SUTURE MATERIAL      FIBROADENOMA  MICROSCOPIC      THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT   REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY      FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE INCLUDING CYST FORMATION  EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  APOCRINE METAPLASIA  AND FIBROSIS      INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMATA  MICROSCOPIC      MICROCALCIFICATIONS      THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Leonard Atkins  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 09                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received is a 36 x 25 x 6cm simple mastectomy specimen with an overlying 25 x 12cm ellipse of skin with a slightly off center  5 5cm areola with a central 1cm nipple  The skin is unremarkable except for a vague REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm portion of puckering  1 8cm from a lateral resection margin  Deep to this area of puckering is a 3 3cm cavity  0 8cm deep  filled with friable  white red tissue and lined by 0 4cm thick  rubbery  white tissue  Thin  red fluid is also present in the biopsy cavity  The biopsy cavity is present 0 8cm from a lateral resection margin  Sectioning the remainder of the breast tissue reveals adipose tissue with admixed white fibrous bands and focal areas of rubbery  white strands of tissue  SECTION CODE  A   representative section of lateral resection margin B C   representative sections of end resection margins D   representative section of deep resection margin closest to biopsy cavity E   representative section of nipple and areola F G   representative sections of biopsy cavity nearest lateral resection margin H through K   representative sections of biopsy cavity L through O   representative sections of remainder of breast tissue  The second specimen   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name   left breast   is a 30 x 25 x 8cm aggregate of fibroadipose tissue  some pieces of which contain overlying  unremarkable skin  Each piece of tissue is sectioned  revealing fibroadipose tissue with focal areas of white  rubbery tissue  Representative sections submitted in P through V  Resident  Elizabeth Bailey  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  Gregory S Parries  M D  James Warren May Jr   M D  David L Berger  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST PART B  LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Negative.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 53 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast core biopsy  eight core samples obtained                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 40                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 17 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast  are eight fragments of soft  tan tissue  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm which are submitted in toto as A  Gross Description by  Jason Corbin Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Barbara Joyce Nath  M D  Jaime L Kline  M D  Daniel Benjamin Kopans  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT  CORE BIOPSY , Positive.
