s with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 07 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  are two fibrous fragments of breast tissue  2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The tissue is inked and sectioned to reveal fibrous tissue as well as a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm lobulated tan white mass present at the inked margin  Specimen submitted in its entirety in cassettes A through C  with the nodular area in A  Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DX  1  LEFT BREAST   NO LESIONS GROSSLY DEFINITIVE FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Positive.
