Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  15 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  15 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 09 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  75     MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  20    MIXED CRIBRIFORM AND MICROPAPILLARY TYPES  3  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  5   INCLUDING LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU AND ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA WITH PAGETOID SPREAD INTO DUCTS INVOLVED BY DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  4  HYALINIZED FIBROADENOMA  5  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH FIBROSIS  CYST FORMATION  AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA  6  MAMMARY DUCT ECTASIA  7  MICROCALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  The infiltrating carcinoma measures 1 6cm in greatest dimension on histologic section  and focally extends to within a fraction of a millimeter of an inked resection margin  No definite vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Immunohistochemical results for estrogen and progesterone receptors will be reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 24                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 19 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fleshy  ill defined nodule that focally abuts the inked margin  A representative section is frozen as FX 1  now A  the remainder of the nodule is submitted in B through H  additional representative sections are submitted in I and J  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST  INFILTRATING and INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  SCOTT D  URBAN  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Positive.
