taining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 20 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two separate parts  Labeled  left breast  1   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm piece of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm gritty white nodule  abutting inked resection margin  Representative section is frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  The rest of the tumor is submitted in A C  The remainder of the breast biopsy entirely in DandE  Labeled  left breast  2   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm oriented breast biopsy  A small suture with a single knot designates the deep superior margin  the area abutting the specimen  1  This area is inked blue over black  A suture with two knots designates the lateral margin of the specimen  and is now inked green  The superficial resection margin is inked red  The medial resection margin is inked yellow  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a 0 7cm in greatest diameter stellate white firm nodule  within  0 1cm of the superficial  red ink  resection margin  The second nodule is more laterally located  and is 1 4cm in greatest dimension  firm  grossly abutting the anterior resection margin of the specimen  Submitted entirely from medial to lateral in F N with medial  small  nodule entirely in G I  and the larger  lateral  nodule entirely in J H  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                        