al Carcinoma In Situ  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Stains for Receptors  Requested on blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST  LEFT   FINAL SUPERIOR MARGIN    EXCISION  UNREMARKABLE FAT  BREAST  LEFT   FINAL LATERAL MARGIN    EXCISION  PLEOMORPHIC LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The lobular carcinoma cells do not stain for E cadherin  BREAST  LEFT   FINAL MEDIAL MARGIN    EXCISION  MICROINVASIVE PLEOMORPHIC LOBULAR CARCINOMA  RARE SINGLE CELLS  PLEOMORPHIC LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Stains for keratin  p63 protein  calponin  and myosin heavy chain do not disclose myoepithelial cells around the invasive carcinoma cells  BREAST  LEFT   FINAL INFERIOR MARGIN    EXCISION  EXTENSIVE PLEOMORPHIC LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FOCAL  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The lobular carcinoma cells do not stain for E cadherin  Stains for keratin  calponin  p63 protein  and myosin heavy chain do not disclose invasive carcinoma  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Results of immunostains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2  cytokeratin 7  and pankeratin on three tissue levels support the above interpretation  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Unfixed  in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Jean Morrissey  REMOVED_DATE  left sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue containing one lymph node 0 7cm in greatest dimension  which is entirely frozen as FX  1 and submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Unfixed  labeled  Jean Morrissey  REMOVED_DATE  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with three localization wires  a long suture designating the lateral aspect  and a short suture designating the superior aspect  The specimen is inked  superior green  inferior yellow  anterior blue  and posterior black  It conta