Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  14 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  14 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 14 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  REMOVED_DATE CM EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The tumor appears slightly different from the prior tumor in the patient s right breast  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 37                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 33 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast biopsy  is a 6 x 4 x 1 3cm portion of breast tissue which is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 7cm white  ill defined  firm area closely approaching the inked resection margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is fibrofatty and unremarkable  The entire tumor and surrounding areas submitted in cassettes A and B  Representative sections of the uninvolved parenchyma is submitted in cassettes C and D  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  REMOVED_DATE CM MASS SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Negative.
