Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 MAY 97 ACCESSIONED ON  23 MAY 97 at 11 46 CLINICAL DATA  Suspicious aspirate  Recently post partum                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  95    GRADE 3  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING FOCALLY TO AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  5    HIGH GRADE  EXTENDING SLIGHTLY AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  WITH INVOLVEMENT OF SEVERAL LOBULES  NOTE  The tumor has a round  circumscribed border  it largely appears to have been  shelled out   and only focally abutts an inked margin  No definite lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is identified  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  29 MAY 97 at 14 47                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 MAY 97 at 12 38 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of breast  inked and sectioned to reveal REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm well circumscribed white to gray  rubbery mass that extends focally to a resection margin  representative sections are frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen to Cox 5  A fragment is taken for possible research  Section Code  A D  representative sections of mass  E H  representative sections of surrounding abnormal tissue  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     Frozen section diagnosis  1  BREAST  EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  ESTHER OLIVA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Negative.
