REMOVED_DATE noted right  breast with visible retraction of skin around nipple at 11 o clock  4 5cm of  mobile fullness spanning from 9 to 12 o clock  and a small nodule in the skin at  10 o clock  There were no palpable axillary or supraclavicular nodes  Mammogram  on REMOVED_DATE noted right breast with architectural distortion at the site of the  palpable mass with associated microcalcifications  Same day ultrasound showed in  the right breast an irregular spiculated solid mass measuring at least REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE  x 1 7cm  and two right axillary suspicious lymph nodes  Physical exam showed  an approximately 5cm mass in the right upper outer quadrant  Right breast core  biopsy revealed invasive ductal carcinoma  grade 3  see MGH report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     Right breast MRI noted an irregular mass with spiculated margins measuring at  least 5 5cm x 3 8cm x 4 2cm  and adjacent satellite nodules in the upper outer  quadrant  The mass extends to the nipple with retraction andassociated skin  thickening  concerning for an inflammatory component  Mildright axillary  adenopathy  with 2 suspicious nodes  was again noted  Core biopsy of a right  axillary node was positive for metastatic carcinoma  see MGH report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     The patient underwent neoadjuvant chemotherapy  On physical exam REMOVED_DATE and  chest CT REMOVED_DATE  the size of the right breast mass was significantly reduced  but difficult to measure     Gross examination of the right breast mastectomy specimen showed a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x  0 4cm small firm nodule in the upper outer quadrant  and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  stellate gray firm subareolar area  These two lesions were grossly separated by  1 0cm  Histologic examination of the small firm nodule shows a fibrotic round  nodule with central coarse calcification  which may represent a hyalinized  fibroadenoma  Sections of the stellate area show residual invasive and in situ  carcinoma in a background showing changes consistent with treatment effect   Invasive carcinoma consists of infiltrating tumor cell clusters that extend up  to and abut  but do not infiltrate  the fibrotic nodule  The tumor bed  dimensions measure REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm after incorporating histologic findings   Invasive carcinoma shows an average cellularity of approximately 5  with a  minimal in situ component  The pre treatment right breast core biopsy has been  returned to the originating institution and is not available for morphologic  comparison  MGH  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID       One of sixteen axillary lymph nodes contains a 0 1cm micrometastasis  seen on  multiple level sections  and biopsy site changes  The resulting architectural  disruption from the biopsy hinders definitive evaluation for extranodal  extension  Treatment effect is not seen in the other 15 negative nodes     Based on the above findings  the tumor response in the breast is estimated to be  Miller Payne grade 3 of 5  and Residual Cancer Burden calculated to be REMOVED_DATE   RCB II         Electronically Signed Out By Amy Ly MD           By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis  certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or  corrected the diagnosis       PROCEDURES ADDENDA    Hormone Receptor Quantitation  Ordered Date  REMOVED_DATE    B  BREAST MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  RIGHT  S P NEOADJUVANT CHEMOTHERAPY   Block tested   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The invasive tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein   The invasive tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein   The invasive tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 protein     Note   Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive  nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows     The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained     Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained     Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stain