Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 01 CLINICAL DATA                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  95    INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  5    NOTE  The margins appear free of carcinoma  but focally the tumor approaches close to the margin  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is seen  A minor component of the lesion has a tubular pattern  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 18 17                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 16     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast mass  is a 2 x 2 x 1cm fibrofatty piece of tissue with a needle localization wire  The external surface is inked and sectioning reveals a firm  poorly defined  gray white tumor  measuring 0 8cm in greatest diameter  A small piece of tissue is taken as frozen section  1 and the block is kept frozen  The remainder of the tissue is submitted in cassettes A E  Gross Description by  C  Diana Jordan  MD Resident  David Andrews  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST   LEFT  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Positive.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 AUG 95 ACCESSIONED ON  08 AUG 95 at 13 18 CLINICAL DATA  61 year old woman with an excisional biopsy of a right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA 70   SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE I III   PRESENT AT SEVERAL INKED SURFACES   SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  30    CRIBRIFORM AND MICROPAPILLARY TYPES WITH COMEDO TYPE NECROSIS  PRESENT AT SEVERAL MARGINS   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Unequivocal lymphatic and vascular invasion is not seen  The invasive carcinoma forms a dominant mass which is 0 8cm  however a microscopic focus of invasive ductal carcinoma is present 0 4cm from the main tumor mass  thus the carcinoma spans 1 2cm  The majority of the ductal carcinoma is within the invasive carcinoma component  however a small percentage   5   of the ductal carcinoma in situ is present away from the main tumor mass  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  10 AUG 95 at 15 49                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 AUG 95 at 07 26 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of breast  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm firm  gray to white  stellate nodule extending to the inked surface  A representative section frozen as FX 1  The entire specimen is submitted in A through F  A and B contains the suspicious nodule   The frozen was saved frozen  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Kenneth Kenji Tanabe  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Positive.
