rs that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is inked  and sectioned to reveal a 2 0cm nodule with multilobulated surface and areas of friable tan tissue admixed with firm white tissue  Representative sections frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remaining tissue submitted entirely in A through M  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED INVASIVE CARCINOMA O R  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY   report_end  , Negative.
